{"name":"Caveman","hex":"#625c58","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"caveman","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An early human or closely related species, popularly held to reside in caves.","A person with backward, primitive behavior, opinions, or interests.\n\n A brutish person, one who behaves in a rough, uncivilized way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caveman"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caveman","blocks":[{"text":"The caveman is a stock character representative of primitive humans in the Paleolithic. The popularization of the type dates to the early 20th century, when Neanderthals were influentially described as \"simian\" or \"ape-like\" by Marcellin Boule and Arthur Keith."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Neanderthal_Flintworkers_%28Knight%2C_1920%29.jpg/330px-Neanderthal_Flintworkers_%28Knight%2C_1920%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caveman","wikidata":"Q1190089"},{"title":"Caveman (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Caveman is a 1981 slapstick comedy film written and directed by Carl Gottlieb and starring Ringo Starr, Dennis Quaid, Shelley Long and Barbara Bach. The film is set during prehistory and revolves around the rivalries between cavemen. The film is an international co-production between Mexico and the United States."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/Caveman_Movie_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caveman_(film)","wikidata":"Q1051862"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Caveman_1.jpg/500px-Caveman_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Caveman_1.jpg/500px-Caveman_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna